      "sentences": [
        {
          "generated_prob": 0.02273140121113912,
          "sentence": "The paper presents a method for training a generative model via an iterative denoising procedure.",
          "perplexity": 0,
          "class_probabilities": {
            "human": 0.9772685987888609,
            "ai": 0.022657236117507383,
            "paraphrased": 0.0000741650936317352
          },
          "interpretability_value": null,
          "interpretability_normalized_value": null,
          "interpretability_designation": null,
          "interpretability_alpha": null,
          "highlight_sentence_for_ai": false,
          "special_highlight_type": null
        },
        {
          "generated_prob": 0.022344849884592538,
          "sentence": "The denoising process is initialized with a random sample from a crude approximation of the data distribution and produces a high-quality sample via multiple denoising steps.",
          "perplexity": 0,
          "class_probabilities": {
            "human": 0.9776551501154075,
            "ai": 0.022271113816693066,
            "paraphrased": 0.00007373606789947235
          },
          "interpretability_value": null,
          "interpretability_normalized_value": null,
          "interpretability_designation": null,
          "interpretability_alpha": null,
          "highlight_sentence_for_ai": false,
          "special_highlight_type": null
        },
        {
          "generated_prob": 0.019712578960656583,
          "sentence": "Training is performed by setting up a Markov chain that slowly blends proposals from the current denoising model with a real example from the data distribution; using this chain, the current denoising model is updated toward reproducing the changed, “better” samples from the blending process.",
          "perplexity": 0,
          "class_probabilities": {
            "human": 0.9802874210393434,
            "ai": 0.019651253738079195,
            "paraphrased": 0.00006132522257738636
          },
          "interpretability_value": null,
          "interpretability_normalized_value": null,
          "interpretability_designation": null,
          "interpretability_alpha": null,
          "highlight_sentence_for_ai": false,
          "special_highlight_type": null
        },
        {
          "generated_prob": 0.014690749563189998,
          "sentence": "This is a clearly written paper that considers an interesting approach to training generative models.",
          "perplexity": 0,
          "class_probabilities": {
            "human": 0.98530925043681,
            "ai": 0.014635045234834212,
            "paraphrased": 0.000055704328355785996
          },
          "interpretability_value": null,
          "interpretability_normalized_value": null,
          "interpretability_designation": null,
          "interpretability_alpha": null,
          "highlight_sentence_for_ai": false,
          "special_highlight_type": null
        },
        {
          "generated_prob": 0.011166300772302446,
          "sentence": "I was intrigued by the simplicity of the presented approach and really enjoyed reading the paper.",
          "perplexity": 0,
          "class_probabilities": {
            "human": 0.9888336992276976,
            "ai": 0.011121148879926566,
            "paraphrased": 0.00004515189237588022
          },
          "interpretability_value": null,
          "interpretability_normalized_value": null,
          "interpretability_designation": null,
          "interpretability_alpha": null,
          "highlight_sentence_for_ai": false,
          "special_highlight_type": null
        },
        {
          "generated_prob": 0.01310169962855934,
          "sentence": "The proposed method is novel, although it has clear ties to other recent work aiming to use denoising models for sampling from distributions, such as the work by Sohl-Dickstein and the recent work on using DAEs as generative models.",
          "perplexity": 0,
          "class_probabilities": {
            "human": 0.9868983003714407,
            "ai": 0.013049046187363774,
            "paraphrased": 0.00005265344119556542
          },
          "interpretability_value": null,
          "interpretability_normalized_value": null,
          "interpretability_designation": null,
          "interpretability_alpha": null,
          "highlight_sentence_for_ai": false,
          "special_highlight_type": null
        },
        {
          "generated_prob": 0.011012405444137596,
          "sentence": "I think this general direction of research is important.",
          "perplexity": 0,
          "class_probabilities": {
            "human": 0.9889875945558624,
            "ai": 0.01096654556854184,
            "paraphrased": 0.000045859875595756825
          },
          "interpretability_value": null,
          "interpretability_normalized_value": null,
          "interpretability_designation": null,
          "interpretability_alpha": null,
          "highlight_sentence_for_ai": false,
          "special_highlight_type": null
        },
        {
          "generated_prob": 0.010246624227683779,
          "sentence": "The proposed procedure takes inspiration from the perspective of generating samples by minimizing an energy function via transitions along a Markov chain and, if successful, could potentially sidestep many problems of current procedures for training directed generative models, such as:",
          "perplexity": 0,
          "class_probabilities": {
            "human": 0.9897533757723163,
            "ai": 0.01020020506749277,
            "paraphrased": 0.000046419160191008384
          },
          "interpretability_value": null,
          "interpretability_normalized_value": null,
          "interpretability_designation": null,
          "interpretability_alpha": null,
          "highlight_sentence_for_ai": false,
          "special_highlight_type": null
        },
        {
          "generated_prob": 0.012701356475953694,
          "sentence": "- convergence and mode coverage problems, as in generative adversarial networks",
          "perplexity": 0,
          "class_probabilities": {
            "human": 0.9872986435240463,
            "ai": 0.012648248738744792,
            "paraphrased": 0.00005310773720890175
          },
          "interpretability_value": null,
          "interpretability_normalized_value": null,
          "interpretability_designation": null,
          "interpretability_alpha": null,
          "highlight_sentence_for_ai": false,
          "special_highlight_type": null
        },
        {
          "generated_prob": 0.011693899123721093,
          "sentence": "- problems with modeling multi-modal distributions, which can arise when a too-restrictive approximate inference model is paired with a powerful generative model",
          "perplexity": 0,
          "class_probabilities": {
            "human": 0.9883061008762789,
            "ai": 0.011644485356378154,
            "paraphrased": 0.00004941376734293839
          },
          "interpretability_value": null,
          "interpretability_normalized_value": null,
          "interpretability_designation": null,
          "interpretability_alpha": null,
          "highlight_sentence_for_ai": false,
          "special_highlight_type": null
        },
        {
          "generated_prob": 0.012779999900276675,
          "sentence": "That being said, another method that seems promising for addressing these issues, and that also has some superficial similarity to the presented work, is the idea of combining Hamiltonian Monte Carlo inference with variational inference, as in [1].",
          "perplexity": 0,
          "class_probabilities": {
            "human": 0.9872200000997233,
            "ai": 0.01272677567269364,
            "paraphrased": 0.00005322422758303572
          },
          "interpretability_value": null,
          "interpretability_normalized_value": null,
          "interpretability_designation": null,
          "interpretability_alpha": null,
          "highlight_sentence_for_ai": false,
          "special_highlight_type": null
        },
        {
          "generated_prob": 0.013856476113313585,
          "sentence": "As such, I am not entirely convinced that the method presented here will be able to perform better than the mentioned paper, although it might be simpler to train.",
          "perplexity": 0,
          "class_probabilities": {
            "human": 0.9861435238866865,
            "ai": 0.01380360863814945,
            "paraphrased": 0.000052867475164134595
          },
          "interpretability_value": null,
          "interpretability_normalized_value": null,
          "interpretability_designation": null,
          "interpretability_alpha": null,
          "highlight_sentence_for_ai": false,
          "special_highlight_type": null
        },
        {
          "generated_prob": 0.0133808209073117,
          "sentence": "Similarly, although I agree that using an MCMC chain to generate samples via an MC-EM-like procedure is likely very costly, I am not convinced such a procedure would not also work reasonably well for the simple MNIST example.",
          "perplexity": 0,
          "class_probabilities": {
            "human": 0.9866191790926883,
            "ai": 0.013323309893605086,
            "paraphrased": 0.00005751101370661364
          },
          "interpretability_value": null,
          "interpretability_normalized_value": null,
          "interpretability_designation": null,
          "interpretability_alpha": null,
          "highlight_sentence_for_ai": false,
          "special_highlight_type": null
        },
        {
          "generated_prob": 0.00017114249559467174,
          "sentence": "In general, a more direct comparison between different inference methods using an MCMC-chain-like procedure would be nice to have, but I understand that this is perhaps outside the scope of this paper.",
          "perplexity": 0,
          "class_probabilities": {
            "human": 0.9998288575044053,
            "ai": 0.00013006642076447954,
            "paraphrased": 0.00004107607483019219
          },
          "interpretability_value": null,
          "interpretability_normalized_value": null,
          "interpretability_designation": null,
          "interpretability_alpha": null,
          "highlight_sentence_for_ai": false,
          "special_highlight_type": null
        },
        {
          "generated_prob": 0.00011849136749098461,
          "sentence": "One thing that I would have expected, however, is a direct comparison to the procedure from Sohl-Dickstein in terms of sampling steps and generation quality, as it is so directly related.",
          "perplexity": 0,
          "class_probabilities": {
            "human": 0.999881508632509,
